### Get all customers

GET http://localhost:5000/api/customers
Content-Type: application/json

### Get customer with id

GET http://localhost:5000/api/customers/1
Content-Type: application/json

### Create customer WITH PASSWORD

POST http://localhost:5000/api/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "customer25@example.com",
  "first_name": "Alex",
  "last_name": "Smith",
  "password": "root",
  "phone": "+12025550129"
}

### Create customer

POST http://localhost:5000/api/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "customer@example.com",
  "first_name": "Alex",
  "last_name": "Smith",
  "phone": "+12025550123"
}

### Update customer WITH PASSWORD

PUT http://localhost:5000/api/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": 1,
  "email": "customer.updated7@example.com",
  "password": "root",
  "first_name": "Alex",
  "last_name": "Smith",
  "phone": "+12025550123"
}


### Update customer

PUT http://localhost:5000/api/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": 1,
  "email": "customer.updated@example.com",
  "first_name": "Alex",
  "last_name": "Smith",
  "phone": "+12025550123"
}

### Delete customer with id

DELETE http://localhost:5000/api/customers/1
Content-Type: application/json
